FX  - In addition to the cited literature, I accessed several datasets to gather the time series data. These included the FAO capture production database for Japanese sardine catches since 1950, Korea Meteorological Administration and Japan Meteorological Agency websites to compile numbers of Asian dust days, European Centre for Medium-Range Weather Forecasts ERA-40 and ERA-Interim reanalysis for ocean precipitation data, NOAA Earth System Research Laboratory ICOADS analysis for SST data, and the Asian-Pacific Data-Research Centre SODA reanalysis for mixed-layer depth of the Kuroshio Extension. The time series of ocean precipitation, SST, and mixed-layer depth were retrieved using the Climate Explorer of the Royal Netherlands Meteorological Institute. This study was funded by the China Ministry of Science and Technology under Grant No. 2013BAD13B06 and logistically supported by the Key Laboratory for South China Sea Fisheries Resources Utilization, China Ministry of Agriculture.
