AB  - The article is devoted to the issues of carbon dioxide removal on underwater vehicles equipped with a power plant based on low-temperature fuel cells (FC). To achieve this goal, options for removing carbon dioxide from the working gas by absorption and adsorption methods are considered. It has been established that seawater can be used as an absorbent due to the high solubility of carbon dioxide. On the basis of physico-chemical processes occurring in the volume of the absorber, the dependences are obtained. It is established that the process of carbon dioxide absorption by a liquid occurs due to the difference in the concentrations of carbon dioxide in the bubble and the surrounding liquid, for this reason, it is necessary to determine the mass transfer surface consisting of the sum of the surfaces of all gas bubbles in the volume of the absorber to determine the effectiveness of the absorber. For increase the degree of purification of hydrogen and its drying after the absorber, adsorption with zeolites can be used.
